</code></pre>

Q: How to get sound out of my quad cortex in linux? A: <p>Found the answer:</p>
<ol>
<li><p><strong>PipeWire 1.4.x</strong></p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>WirePlumber</strong></p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Neural DSP Quad Cortex</strong> in <em>Pro Audio</em> profile</p>
<p><code>nano ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/quad-aux23.conf</code><br />
In this file, paste:</p>
<pre><code>context.modules = [
  { name = libpipewire-module-loopback
    args = {
      node.name = &quot;quad-aux23&quot;
      node.description = &quot;Quad Cortex AUX 2-3&quot;

      capture.props = {
        media.class = &quot;Audio/Sink&quot;
        audio.channels = 2
        audio.position = [ FL FR ]
      }

      playback.props = {
        node.target = &quot;alsa_output.usb-Neural_DSP_Quad_Cortex-00.pro-output-0&quot;

        audio.channels = 2
        audio.position = [ AUX2 AUX3 ]

        stream.dont-remix = true
        node.passive = true
      }
    }
  }
]
</code></pre>
</li>
</ol>
<p>Then: <code>systemctl --user restart pipewire pipewire-pulse wireplumber</code></p>
<p>and <code>wpctl set-default input.quad-aux23</code></p>
